        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#64748b;fontSize=16;spacing=10;align=left;fontSize=16;" value="&lt;b&gt;What this tells us&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The two SG108s and the SX105 do not provide configurable per-port VLAN separation.&lt;br&gt;The bookshelf-to-desk cable is shared by every desk device.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lower-change option:&lt;/b&gt; if every device behind the bookshelf can join Yesod, dedicate that router port to Yesod&lt;br&gt;and keep both SG108s. This alone does not move Sefer’s guests into the same VLAN.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The previously reported DHCP issue needs fresh diagnosis; creating a VLAN is not itself a proven fix." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="1175" x="35" y="820" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
