        <mxCell id="4pOgHDq0Nz2RlTCsoZjO-24" parent="4pOgHDq0Nz2RlTCsoZjO-1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#64748b;fontSize=16;spacing=10;align=left;fontSize=16;" value="&lt;b&gt;Traffic crosses the ER7206 under explicit rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;pompom → Yesod: management access • Yesod → NAS: required storage services&lt;br&gt;Return traffic allowed; other cross-VLAN access restricted. Use DNS across VLANs; do not assume .local discovery.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*Sefer:&lt;/b&gt; VLAN-aware host bridge / VM NICs; management can remain on the trusted LAN.&lt;br&gt;Desk devices share one VLAN in this design. Separate management or guest VLANs at the desk require a managed desk switch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tradeoff:&lt;/b&gt; cross-VLAN storage traffic takes the router’s gigabit path. This drawing is a proposal, not deployed configuration." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="1175" x="35" y="820" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
